MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Mamas & the Papas felt like a natural choice because warm harmonies and melodic folk-rock connect with the older, roots-oriented music I have been choosing.",
    "Sgt. Pepper's appealed to me through its memorable songwriting and melodic arrangements, which fit my recent interest in veteran rock musicians."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The metal, rap-rock and pop-punk choices emphasize aggression and intensity, while I currently want bluesy playing, warmth and roots-oriented songs.",
    "Appetite for Destruction has some blues-rock connections, but its forceful energy outweighs that similarity for me. Being mellow is not enough either: Parachutes and 25 do not offer the musical connection I am seeking today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat very different kinds of rock as interchangeable, even though their sound and energy strongly affect whether I would choose them.",
    "The list seems to lean on widely familiar albums more than on what connects them to my recent listening; familiarity alone would not make me interact."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent choices point toward blues, roots-oriented music and veteran musicians, where expressive playing and songcraft matter more to me than heaviness.",
    "I can enjoy melodic older rock beyond blues, but the warmth and feel need to connect; a shared rock label or a softer sound alone is not enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in older rock, but stretched it too broadly into heavier and less roots-oriented music."
}
